      "writtenOn": "2024-04-19T06:47:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this would be easier to use if automatically retrieves the required battery info. Let me do this in the next CL.\n\n---\n\nOn the other hand, I think it\u0027 better to make `index` required in `ectool bcfg set`.\n\nIn `ectool bcfg get`, if index is not specified, it means to get the active battery config.\n\nIn `ectool bcfg set`, if index is not specified, it means to set the battery config to index 0.\n\nThe inconsistency might be confusing. Let\u0027s make index required in ` ectool bcfg set` since we don\u0027t set the active battery config by not specifying the index.",
      "parentUuid": "4e5516c8_6b5108f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8582,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 8582,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "44bca75528896d5b4f785600c75d6c8c7e1cabf6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a5a605d_ba019866",
        "filename": "util/ectool.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 8582,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-19T18:45:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If an index isn\u0027t specified for `bcfg set`, how about doing the following?\n\n* If a config for the given manuf_name,device_name already exists in CBI, that\u0027ll be the index to be used.\n* If a config doesn\u0027t exist, the first available slot will be used.\n\nThis way, we\u0027ll be able to avoid human errors of adding duplicate configs. (FYI: when two configs exist in CBI for the same battery, the first entry will be used. That is,  bcfg set 1 succeeds but the config will never be used if slot 0 has another config for the same battery.)",
      "parentUuid": "798f1a41_73ff6e25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8582,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 8582,
        "endChar": 58
      },
